@@ -305,3 +305,22 @@ pass0_post, проходы модели 1..12 (за каждым `_post`, обн
 **Поправка к A/B выше («кадр упирается в CPU»).** Те замеры шли, пока 12 зависших процессов
 shadPS4 занимали по ядру. На свободной системе: «host copies» 1.6%, ожидание GPU ~41% — кадр
 упирается в GPU, так что async compute для FSR снова имеет смысл.
+
+## MetalFX frame interpolation (macOS 26+, 2026-10-21)
+
+`BB_METALFX_INTERPOLATE=1` with `upscaler=metalfx` shows a MetalFX-interpolated
+frame between every two real ones (`gpu/shim/bbport_metalfx.mm`
+`Interpolator`, `vk_metalfx.cpp` `MetalFxUpscaler::Interpolate`,
+`vk_presenter.cpp`). Inputs: the frame as presented (blitted to RGBA16F) and the
+previous one, with this frame's depth and motion vectors from the MetalFX
+temporal scaler's staging buffers (the scaler must have run this frame). The
+interpolator is not chained to the scaler: at Native AA the scaler's output
+precedes post-processing and the HUD, and a HUD-less frame between HUD frames
+would flicker. The presenter shows the interpolated frame first and the real one
+half a measured frame interval later (exponential average of real intervals),
+so every frame arrives half an interval late. The HUD is interpolated with the
+scene (`uiTexture` is nil): expect ghosting on moving HUD elements. The camera's
+far plane is not read from the game (10,000 is passed); near and the vertical
+field of view come from `CameraMotion`. The frame log gains a `presented`
+column (presents per flip, 1 or 2). Failures switch interpolation off with one
+`Upscaler: MetalFX frame interpolation off (...)` line; the game goes on.
